123	## 3. Error handling
124	
125	`src/Utils/request/errorHandler.ts` exports `handleHttpError(error: Error)`. Wired globally in `src/Utils/request/queryClient.ts`:
126	
127	```ts
128	const queryClient = new QueryClient({
129	  defaultOptions: { queries: { retry: false, refetchOnWindowFocus: false } },
130	  queryCache: new QueryCache({ onError: handleHttpError }),
131	  mutationCache: new MutationCache({ onError: handleHttpError }),
132	});
133	// module augmentation: Register { defaultError: HTTPError; queryMeta: QueryMeta }
134	```
135	
136	`HTTPError` (in `src/Utils/request/types.ts`): `class HTTPError extends Error { status: number; silent: boolean; cause?: StructuredError | Record<string, unknown> | undefined }` — thrown by `callApi` when `!res.ok`, with `cause` = parsed response body. `StructuredError = Record<string, string | string[]>`.
137	
138	Handler flow (toast util is **`toast` from `"sonner"`**):
139	- `silent: true` (or `silent(response) => true`) on `ApiCallOptions` → `handleHttpError` returns immediately (`if (("silent" in error && error.silent) || error.name === "AbortError") return;`). QuestionnaireForm uses this to take over batch error rendering: `mutationFn: mutate(batchApi.batchRequest, { silent: true })`.
140	- 404 → `toast.error(cause?.detail || t("not_found"))`; 413 → `t("file_too_large")`.
141	- session expiry (`cause.code === "token_not_valid"` or `detail === "Authentication credentials were not provided."`) → `navigate("/session-expired?redirect=...")`.
142	- 400/406 (`isBadRequest`): handles three shapes — array of `{errors: PydanticError[]}`, `cause.errors` as `PydanticError[]` (`{type, loc?, msg, input?, url?}`; toasts `msg` with `description: "${Type}: '${loc.join(".")}'"`, duration 8000), or `StructuredError` (toasts each string/array value; for object entries picks first of `["detail","msg","error","message"]`). Fallback: `Notifications.BadRequest({ errs })` from `src/Utils/Notifications.ts` (deprecated, sonner-based).
143	- Everything else → `toast.error(cause?.detail || t("something_went_wrong"))`.
144	
145	So a mutation that renders its own field-level errors should pass `{ silent: true }` and parse `error.cause` in `onError`.
