281	## Minimal adapter interface wrapping ALL 12 unchanged
282	
283	```ts
284	import type { ComponentType } from "react";
285	
286	import type { StructuredQuestionType } from "@/components/Questionnaire/data/StructuredFormData";
287	import type { QuestionValidationError } from "@/types/questionnaire/batch";
288	import type {
289	  QuestionnaireResponse,
290	  ResponseValue,
291	} from "@/types/questionnaire/form";
292	import type { Question } from "@/types/questionnaire/question";
293	
294	/** Exactly what QuestionInput's commonProps supplies today (minus context ids). */
295	export interface StructuredQuestionBaseProps {
296	  question: Question;
297	  questionnaireResponse: QuestionnaireResponse;
298	  updateQuestionnaireResponseCB: (
299	    values: ResponseValue[],
300	    questionId: string,
301	    note?: string,
302	  ) => void;
303	  errors: QuestionValidationError[];
304	  clearError: () => void;
305	  disabled?: boolean;
306	  withLabel?: boolean;
307	  index: number;
308	  classes?: string;
309	  disableRightBorder?: boolean;
310	  questionnaireId?: string;
311	  questionnaireSlug?: string;
312	}
313	
314	export type StructuredContextKey = "encounterId" | "facilityId";
315	
316	export interface StructuredQuestionContext {
317	  patientId: string; // always available (required QuestionInput prop)
318	  encounterId?: string;
319	  facilityId?: string;
320	}
321	
322	/** Props delivered to a component whose required context keys R are verified present. */
323	export type StructuredQuestionProps<R extends StructuredContextKey = never> =
324	  StructuredQuestionBaseProps &
325	    Omit<StructuredQuestionContext, R> &
326	    Required<Pick<StructuredQuestionContext, R>>;
327	
328	export interface StructuredQuestionAdapter<
329	  R extends StructuredContextKey = never,
330	> {
331	  structuredType: StructuredQuestionType;
332	  /** Gate: all listed ids must be truthy before rendering Component. */
333	  requiredContext: readonly R[];
334	  /** i18n key rendered as <span>{t(key)}</span> when the gate fails. */
335	  missingContextKey: string;
336	  Component: ComponentType<StructuredQuestionProps<R>>;
337	}
338	
339	export type AnyStructuredQuestionAdapter =
340	  | StructuredQuestionAdapter<never>
341	  | StructuredQuestionAdapter<"encounterId">
342	  | StructuredQuestionAdapter<"facilityId">
343	  | StructuredQuestionAdapter<"encounterId" | "facilityId">;
344	```
345	
346	Per-type instantiations that type-check against the existing components with zero changes (contravariant props check passes because `StructuredQuestionProps<R>` is a supertype-widening superset of each component's declared props):
347	
348	- `StructuredQuestionAdapter<never>`: `time_of_death` (missingContextKey unused).
349	- `StructuredQuestionAdapter<"encounterId">`: `medication_request`, `medication_statement`, `allergy_intolerance` (gate-only; component ignores the id), `symptom`, `diagnosis`.
350	- `StructuredQuestionAdapter<"facilityId">`: `appointment`.
351	- `StructuredQuestionAdapter<"encounterId" | "facilityId">`: `service_request`, `charge_item`, `encounter`, `files` (files gates on both today, uses only encounterId).
352	
353	Registry + renderer replacing the switch:
354	
355	```ts
356	export const structuredQuestionAdapters: Record<
357	  StructuredQuestionType,
358	  AnyStructuredQuestionAdapter
359	> = { /* 11 entries as tabulated above */ };
360	
361	function renderStructuredQuestion(
362	  adapter: AnyStructuredQuestionAdapter,
363	  base: StructuredQuestionBaseProps,
364	  context: StructuredQuestionContext,
365	  t: (key: string) => string,
366	) {
367	  if (adapter.requiredContext.some((key) => !context[key])) {
368	    return <span>{t(adapter.missingContextKey)}</span>;
369	  }
370	  const Component = adapter.Component as ComponentType<
371	    StructuredQuestionProps<never>
372	  >;
373	  return <Component {...base} {...context} />;
374	}
375	```
376	
377	The single `as` cast is required because TS cannot correlate the runtime `requiredContext` guard with the union's type parameter (a discriminated-union narrowing on `structuredType` per-entry would avoid it at the cost of 11 literal branches). One behavioral delta to preserve: `symptom` currently re-passes `patientId` explicitly (a no-op — already in commonProps), and `allergy_intolerance`/`files` gate on ids they never receive — the adapter's gate-vs-props split (`requiredContext` gates; spread passes all context) reproduces both exactly.

